// Tool objects for tools/list: descriptions + inputSchemas are verbatim
// from the python live capture (tools/list id=2); `do` is present (P2
// seam). Post-capture sentences appended to the descriptions document
// element fp, stale_ref, and the UIPI errors; no captured text was edited.
// P2a: `_meta.fastmcp.tags` noise removed and every tool carries a real
// `outputSchema` matching its `structuredContent` (the python capture's
// `x-fastmcp-wrap-result` string wrapper is gone).
pub const TOOL_SCREENSHOT: &str = r#"{"description": "Capture the screen for a vision model. display=-1 whole virtual\ndesktop, 0..N one monitor (out of range -> error). window=<selector>\ncaptures that window side-effect-free (never restored/raised/focused)\nand wins over display. Selector grammar: \"123456\"|\"hwnd:123456\" hwnd,\n\"pid:<int>\", \"exe:<name>\" (with/without .exe), \"title:<substr>\",\n\"class:<name>\" (disambiguator), or bare text (= titleContains). window=\nis parsed with the same TargetSpec grammar as target=, so the two differ\nonly in spelling and both carry the full lock (pid, creation time, image,\nclass, revalidated). region=[left,top,right,bottom]\nin virtual-desktop px applies after the window crop. max_px (default\n1280) is a long-edge clamp, aspect-preserving, never upscaling; null\nreturns native pixels. fmt png|jpeg (jpg is an alias for jpeg); JPEG\nquality is clamped to 1-100, PNG ignores quality. grid=true overlays a\nlight 128px lattice. allow_crop_fallback=true permits a foreground-only\ndesktop crop to dwm_rect when PrintWindow refuses (default refuses).\nelements=true appends a THIRD content block: a compact JSON object\n{backend,truncated,rect_space,elements,uia_available,uia_error,\nfallback,empty,depth_capped,depth_limit} where elements lists the\nwindow's controls as {win,hwnd,role,name,auto_id,rect:[l,t,w,h],\noffscreen,invokable,path}. offscreen:true marks a control with no on-screen\narea (rect kept for shape, not geometry to aim at). rect is in SCREEN coordinates so it composes with the\nsame coordinate_map formula above (source.x/y origin, source.w/h over\nimage.w/h). Anonymous layout nodes (no name, no auto_id, not\ninvokable) are dropped; the list caps at 200 entries with\ntruncated:true. backend names which element backend served this call:\n\"uia\" (native UIAutomation COM walk) or\n\"win32\" (EnumChildWindows/GetWindowText/GetClassName/GetWindowRect\nfallback when UIA yields nothing). An empty list is reported, not\nimplied: empty:true with an empty_reason, plus uia_available (was UIA\neven loadable) and fallback (which fallback ran). When the UIA\nrecursion cut-off (depth_limit 8) actually hides deeper controls,\ndepth_capped:true is set and truncated is true. With window=<selector>\nthe model covers that window, otherwise the current foreground window.\nWith display/region + elements=true the image is the desktop/monitor/region\nwhile the element block still describes the FOREGROUND window; the payload\nnames it in elements_window{hwnd,exe,title} so the two are never confused.\n\nReturns [image, coordinate_map_json] plus the element block when\nelements=true. Map model image px back with:\nscreen_x = source.x + round((img_x + 0.5) * source.w / image.w)\n(same for y). For window captures source.x/y equal the dwm_rect origin\nand source.kind is \"window\". A window that moves during the capture sets\ncapture.moved_during_capture:true and source.x/y report the POST-capture DWM\norigin (a pure translation is recaptured once), so a stale origin is never\npresented as current. Zoom path for small targets: pass a tight\nwindow/region with max_px=1280. out=<absolute path> also writes the exact\nreturned bytes to disk (parent dirs created, PNG when out is set and fmt\nis omitted since a diff needs lossless pixels) and adds\nout:{path,bytes,fmt} to the payload; a write failure refuses the call. Errors: [\"error: <code>: <detail>\"]\nwith codes bad_display|bad_region|bad_window|ambiguous_window|\nempty_crop|capture_failed|ambiguous_target|target_gone|window_minimized|\ncapture_unavailable|bad_out. Never raises.\n\nBackground-safe by default, target-locked: target={hwnd?,pid?,exe?,appId?,\ntitleContains?,className?} (or a selector string) resolves ONE top-level\nwindow for this call and wins over window=. The window is captured with\nPrintWindow(PW_RENDERFULLCONTENT) WITHOUT activating, raising, restoring or\nmoving the pointer - the lock is revalidated (IsWindow, pid, image name,\nclass, AppUserModelID) and survives the user alt-tabbing away. Ambiguous or\nvanished targets are typed errors (ambiguous_target / target_gone) and NEVER\nfall back to the foreground window. A minimized window returns\nwindow_minimized and is never restored; a refused or blank/black PrintWindow\nframe returns capture_unavailable with the reason. Objects/lists in the\nmap: foregroundUnchanged and cursorUnchanged carry the measured before/after\ninvariant (telemetry; the guarantee is that the capture path has no\nactivation call at all).\nElements entries (elements=true block) also carry fp, a stable identity\nfingerprint per control - see the elements tool; pass it as expect_fp to\ninvoke/set_value to refuse stale refs instead of acting on the wrong control.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"target": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hwnd": {"type": "integer"}, "pid": {"type": "integer"}, "exe": {"type": "string"}, "appId": {"type": "string"}, "titleContains": {"type": "string"}, "className": {"type": "string"}}}, {"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "display": {"type": "integer", "default": -1}, "region": {"anyOf": [{"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "window": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "max_px": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 8192}, {"type": "null"}], "default": 1280}, "fmt": {"type": "string", "enum": ["png", "jpeg", "jpg"], "default": "jpeg"}, "quality": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 100, "default": 80}, "grid": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "allow_crop_fallback": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "elements": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "out": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}}}, "name": "screenshot", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"image": {"type": "object"}, "source": {"type": "object"}, "scale": {"type": "number"}, "monitors": {"type": "object"}, "cursor": {"type": "object"}, "window": {"type": "object"}, "capture": {"type": "object"}, "formula": {"type": "string"}, "foregroundUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "cursorUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["image", "source", "scale", "monitors", "cursor", "capture", "formula"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Screenshot", "annotations": {"title": "Screenshot", "readOnlyHint": true, "destructiveHint": false, "idempotentHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_DIFF: &str = r#"{"description": "Pixel diff for \"only the intended pixels changed\": compare two captures and report exactly which pixels moved. Each of base/next is either {path:\"<png>\"} (an absolute .png path, decoded as-is) or a capture target ({target|window, display, region} with the same selector grammar as screenshot; captured side-effect-free at native pixels, never activated or raised). Both sides must decode/capture to the SAME pixel dimensions: a mismatch is a typed size_mismatch naming both sizes, never a silent scale. threshold (0-255 per channel, default 0) is the only tolerance; max_px (default 1280) is a long-edge clamp for the returned diff image, aspect-preserving, never upscaling; out writes the diff PNG to an absolute path (parents created); bbox (default true) toggles the union box. Returns {changed,total,ratio,bbox:[x,y,w,h]|null,identical,base:{w,h},next:{w,h},threshold,diff_out?}; when anything changed a second content block carries the diff image (changed pixels solid red over a dimmed greyscale copy of base). Read-only: no activation, no input. Errors never raise.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"base": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "string"}]}, "next": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "string"}]}, "threshold": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 255, "default": 0}, "max_px": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 8192}, {"type": "null"}], "default": 1280}, "out": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "bbox": {"type": "boolean", "default": true}}, "required": ["base", "next"]}, "name": "diff", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "changed": {"type": "integer"}, "total": {"type": "integer"}, "ratio": {"type": "number"}, "bbox": {"anyOf": [{"type": "array"}, {"type": "null"}]}, "identical": {"type": "boolean"}, "base": {"type": "object"}, "next": {"type": "object"}, "threshold": {"type": "integer"}, "diff_out": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object"}, {"type": "null"}]}}, "required": ["ok", "changed", "total", "ratio", "identical", "base", "next"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Diff", "annotations": {"title": "Diff", "readOnlyHint": true, "destructiveHint": false, "idempotentHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_LIST_WINDOWS: &str = r#"{"description": "List visible top-level windows as JSON:\n[{hwnd,pid,exe,title,class,rect:[l,t,r,b],dwm_rect,client_rect,\nminimized,maximized,foreground,cloaked,visible,dpi}].\nrect=GetWindowRect (compat, includes the invisible border);\ndwm_rect=DWMWA_EXTENDED_FRAME_BOUNDS (mapping truth, else rect with\ndwm_fallback:true); client_rect in screen space. Read-only: no focus\nchange, no window is touched.\nelevated names the target's integrity: true when its process runs\nelevated (input from this unelevated server is UIPI-blocked: refused\nbefore injecting with uipi_blocked, flagged blocked_by_uipi:true),\nfalse when not elevated, null when unreadable (never named elevated).\ninclude_app_ids (default false) adds appId per window from the window's\nAppUserModelID property store (a string, or null when the store/property is\nunavailable). It is opt-in because that read is a per-window COM call.", "inputSchema": {"properties": {"include_app_ids": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}}, "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}, "name": "list_windows", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"windows": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object"}}}, "required": ["windows"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "List Windows", "annotations": {"title": "List Windows", "readOnlyHint": true, "destructiveHint": false, "idempotentHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_WINDOW: &str = r#"{"description": "Window control. action in focus|move|resize|minimize|maximize|restore|\nclose|topmost. Target by selector (hwnd:|pid:|exe:|title:|class:|bare\ndigits=hwnd, bare text=title/exe search, case-insensitive) or hwnd.\ntitle is a case-insensitive title substring (the same lock as target's\ntitleContains); hwnd is the same lock as target's hwnd. Both carry pid +\nprocess creation time + image + class and are revalidated before the action.\nmove needs x,y; resize needs width,height. Returns JSON {ok,...};\nambiguous matches return ok:false with a candidate list.\n\nNo-steal by default: target={hwnd?,pid?,exe?,appId?,titleContains?,\nclassName?} (or a selector string) locks ONE top-level window for the call\nand wins over title/hwnd; it is revalidated before the action and an\nambiguous/vanished target is typed (ambiguous_target / target_gone, never a\nforeground fallback). action=focus and action=maximize are refused with no_foreground_policy (focusing IS taking the foreground; maximizing covers its monitor and Win32 documents no no-activate form) and the window is untouched. allow_foreground:true refuses the whole call the same way - no flag buys the foreground. move and\nresize use SetWindowPos with SWP_NOACTIVATE, minimize uses\nSW_SHOWMINNOACTIVE, restore uses SW_SHOWNOACTIVATE, maximize resizes to the\nmonitor work area with SWP_NOACTIVATE, topmost adds SWP_NOACTIVATE, and close\nposts WM_CLOSE - none of them activates, raises or moves the pointer.\nforegroundUnchanged/cursorUnchanged report the measured before/after\ninvariant.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"action": {"type": "string", "enum": ["focus", "move", "resize", "minimize", "maximize", "restore", "close", "topmost"]}, "title": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "hwnd": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "x": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "y": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "width": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "height": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "target": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hwnd": {"type": "integer"}, "pid": {"type": "integer"}, "exe": {"type": "string"}, "appId": {"type": "string"}, "titleContains": {"type": "string"}, "className": {"type": "string"}}}, {"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "allow_foreground": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}}, "required": ["action"], "allOf": [{"if": {"properties": {"action": {"const": "move"}}}, "then": {"required": ["x", "y"]}}, {"if": {"properties": {"action": {"const": "resize"}}}, "then": {"required": ["width", "height"]}}]}, "name": "window", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "action": {"type": "string"}, "hwnd": {"type": "integer"}, "x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "width": {"type": "integer"}, "height": {"type": "integer"}, "error": {"type": "string"}, "candidates": {"type": "array"}, "code": {"type": "string"}, "foregroundUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "cursorUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "target_locked": {"type": "integer"}}, "required": ["ok"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Window", "annotations": {"title": "Window", "readOnlyHint": false, "destructiveHint": true, "idempotentHint": false, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_DO: &str = r#"{"description": "BURST tool: execute queued input actions in ONE MCP round-trip.\nAction types: move|click|down|up|drag|scroll|type|key|hotkey|wait|\nwait_for|focus_window|invoke|set_value|clipboard_set|clipboard_get. Background-only: every acting verb is posted to a locked target (PostMessage/UIA) or refused with a typed no_foreground_policy/no_cursor_policy/no_clipboard_policy/background_unavailable error. SendInput is never called; allow_foreground:true and delivery:\"sendinput\" refuse instead of acting. wait/wait_for poll without injecting anything. Returns JSON with per-action {index,type,ok,ms[,mode]}\nplus total_ms, sendinput_calls, sendinput_ms, events, focus_before,\nfocus_after\n(and focus_restored when the guard runs, posted_messages plus\nbackground_note under background). sendinput_calls and sendinput_ms are always 0 (SendInput is never called; the fields stay for envelope compatibility). wait_for waits\nuntil the requested\ncondition is satisfied, polling inside the tool until it reaches a\nsatisfied state or the timeout expires:\n{\"type\":\"wait_for\",\"kind\":\"window_appear|window_disappear|pixel|\nstable|element\",\"selector\":...,\"x\":..,\"y\":..,\"color\":[r,g,b],\"tolerance\":..,\n\"region\":[l,t,r,b],\"timeout_ms\":..,\"poll_ms\":..}. kind:\"element\" waits\nfor a control instead of pixels: {\"window\":...} (optional window selector,\ndefault foreground), \"element\" (required name:|auto_id:|path: selector like\ninvoke), \"state\" appear|disappear|enabled|disabled (default appear). Timeouts\nand cancellation behave like the other kinds.\nA TIMEOUT IS NOT AN\nERROR: it returns ok:true with satisfied:false (the\nsatisfied/unsatisfied flag, never an error) so the rest of a batch\ncontinues; ok:false only for a malformed action. Per-action failures\nnever abort the burst: every action reports its own ok:false and the\nremaining actions still run (continue-always).\nclick on an element (\"element\":\"name:OK|auto_id:..|path:..\") is\nUIA-pattern first (Invoke/SelectionItem/Toggle) with ONE posted button-down +\nbutton-up at the element centre as the fallback (converted from the screen\nrect to exact client pixels; \"fallback\":\"click\" is refused with no_cursor_policy\nunder the background-only policy); hover:true (posted clicks only) is the sole way\nto ask for a WM_MOUSEMOVE. Posted clicks are honest about what they proved:\nevery click result carries delivered (uia|posted) and effect\n(verified|pattern-returned|unchanged|unverified); a posted element click\nwhose readable control state (expanded/value/text/enabled) did not change\nfails with background_unavailable and delivered:\"posted\", and a raw x/y\nclick always reports delivered:\"posted\", effect:\"unverified\". Keyboard/text honesty: type with an element and set_value are refused with background_unavailable naming the element (their UIA ValuePattern.SetValue provider may FOCUS the control) BEFORE any provider call. invoke/toggle/expand/collapse/scroll patterns stay\nbackground-safe. Plain type, key and hotkey are NEVER posted - WM_CHAR/\nWM_KEYDOWN bypass the input queue, desync the target and are ignored by many\ncontrols - so plain type/key/hotkey post to a locked target (delivery:\"auto\"|\"posted\", verified by default with a before/after pixel diff; delivery:\"sendinput\" is refused) and return target_required without one. Posted keyboard to a desktop the server created stays available\n(the desktop:\"hidden\" permission is earned by desktop-name comparison, never\ngranted by the argument alone). scroll axis \"v\"|\"h\" (default \"v\") selects the vertical or horizontal wheel; key holds Shift when the layout (VkKeyScanW high byte) requires it, else a Unicode fallback like type.\nbackground: a window selector (hwnd:|pid:|exe:|title:) delivering click/\ndown/up/drag/scroll by POSTING pointer messages (WM_LBUTTONDOWN/UP,\nWM_MOUSEMOVE, WM_MOUSEWHEEL) to that window with client-area coordinates\nconverted from the usual virtual-desktop px; keyboard verbs are refused\nhere (posted WM_CHAR/WM_KEYDOWN need a locked target) and are refused without one. The target is\nNEVER activated, focused, or raised. BACKGROUND MODE IS BEST-EFFORT:\nPostMessage input is not honoured by every app and is NOT equivalent to\nreal (SendInput) input. drag and scroll are posted to the same target (WM_LBUTTONDOWN /\nWM_MOUSEMOVE / WM_LBUTTONUP and WM_MOUSEWHEEL at the exact point, no\npointer); move has no window-message equivalent and is refused with\nbackground_unavailable instead of silently doing nothing. Every background-delivered action reports mode:\"background\" plus\nthe resolved target hwnd.\ndesktop: opt-in mode string, default null. Only \"hidden\" is accepted; it launches the program named by background (\"exe:notepad.exe\" or a path) on a private hidden desktop, resolves the target window with EnumDesktopWindows (never the owner's EnumWindows), drives it through the PostMessage path above, captures the window with PrintWindow(PW_RENDERFULLCONTENT) and returns the usual burst JSON plus a hidden_desktop object {desktop_created, launched_pid, window_hwnd, window_on_hidden_desktop, absent_from_owner_enum_windows, text_readback, capture{ok,w,h,print_flags,min,max,uniform,bytes,png_b64}, teardown{...}, owner_cursor_delta, owner_foreground_delta}. The owner's cursor, foreground window, and focus are never touched; the launched process is closed and the desktop destroyed before the call returns. Omit desktop for the unchanged default behaviour.\nbackground_args: optional argv for the hidden launch only (array of strings, e.g. a document path to open instead of the app's persisted session); ignored without desktop:\"hidden\".\nfocus_guard: when true and the foreground window changed during the call,\nthe entry foreground window is restored; focus_before/focus_after hwnds\nare always reported, plus focus_restored under the guard.\ninvoke: {\"type\":\"invoke\",\"element\":\"name:OK|auto_id:btnOk|path:0.1.2\",\n\"index\":0} activates one control from the structured element model of\nthe locked target window (a target is required: this server never falls\nback to the foreground window) through the pattern that element\nsupports: UIA Invoke/SelectionItem/Toggle, or a Win32 BM_CLICK under\nthe Win32 element fallback. It never moves the mouse and never changes\nthe foreground, and there is no pixel fallback: \"fallback\":\"click\" is\nrefused with no_cursor_policy because the pointer is never moved. When the selector\nmatches more than one element and no explicit index is given, invoke\ndoes NOT act: it returns ok:false with a candidates list\n[{name,role,auto_id,rect,ref}] so the caller can disambiguate; an explicit\nindex (even 0) acts on the nth match. Every invoke result names its\nactivation path in via\n(uia-invoke|uia-select|uia-toggle|win32-click|none) plus\nthe backend that served the element list and a resolution of\nfound|not-found|ambiguous|list-failed. invoke state \"expand\"|\"collapse\"\ndrives ONLY the UIA ExpandCollapse pattern (typed error without it;\nnever Invoke, so a SplitButton cannot open a menu instead of collapsing);\nthe result names via uia-expand|uia-collapse plus the post-action\nexpand_state (Collapsed|Expanded|PartiallyExpanded|LeafNode).\nset_value: {\"type\":\"set_value\",\"element\":\"name:OK|auto_id:100|path:0\",\n\"text\":\"...\"} writes text into one control from the same element model\nvia UIA ValuePattern.SetValue - no click, no coordinates, but the provider\nMAY focus the control (measured), so set_value is refused with background_unavailable naming the element before any provider\ncall. Selectors are name:|auto_id:|path: only (no ref:); ambiguous\nmatches return ok:false with a candidates list like invoke. Failures are\ntyped ok:false: element not found, element has no ValuePattern, element\nis read-only, or control re-resolution (stale path) failure; the Win32\nfallback has no ValuePattern and fails. Success reports the control accepts no set_value write: UIA text entry may take the\nforeground, so set_value is refused with background_unavailable naming the\nelement before any provider call. The refusal never echoes the text value\n(it may be a password).\ntype posts WM_CHAR per unit to the locked target; chunk_chars/chunk_ms are\naccepted for compatibility but perform no pacing.\ntype also accepts element (name:|auto_id:|path:), index and expect_fp exactly\nlike set_value: with an element it is refused with background_unavailable naming the element; without one it posts WM_CHAR to the locked target.\nBurst budget: at most 256 actions and 300 s of total elapsed time per call.\nExceeding either is a typed burst_budget_exceeded result naming the limit and\nthe actual value, reported like any other per-action failure; the remaining\nactions do not run.\nmove takes x/y (absolute, desktop-clamped) or dx/dy (relative deltas,\n|d|<=32767, no desktop gate, never mixed). key takes hold_ms (0..60000)\nand repeat (1..100, gap_ms between repeats): per repeat the key goes\ndown, flush, hold, up, flush, cancellably; dry_run assembles every\nevent without sleeping. scroll with element name:|auto_id:|path:\ndrives UIA ScrollPattern instead of the wheel (typed error without\nthe pattern); without element it is the plain wheel.\nclipboard: {\"type\":\"clipboard_set\",\"text\":\"...\"} writes CF_UNICODETEXT; {\"type\":\"clipboard_get\"} reads it back\nas {ok,text}. clipboard_set OVERWRITES the owner's global clipboard, a side\neffect outside the target window (every application shares it), so it\nis refused with no_clipboard_policy BEFORE OpenClipboard - a refused call touches nothing. clipboard_get stays\nfree. Clipboard content may hold secrets: treat get results as\nsensitive, never log or paste them beyond the caller.\ndry_run=true validates exactly like the live call (including the policy\nrefusals) but posts nothing\n(metadata is still reported); invoke under dry_run still resolves the\nelement and reports found/not-found/ambiguous plus the path it would\nuse - it just never fires. For headless benchmarking without\ntouching the desktop.\nStale refs: invoke accepts expect_fp (the fp from an elements\nentry); a mismatch refuses with resolution:stale and a stale_ref error\nnaming expected vs found fps - take a fresh elements snapshot and retry.\nCandidates lists carry {name,role,auto_id,rect,ref,fp}; invoke\nresolutions add stale (expect_fp mismatch) and uipi_blocked (elevated\ntarget) to found|not-found|ambiguous|list-failed.\nUIPI/elevation: input aimed at an elevated (higher-integrity) target is\nrefused BEFORE injecting with a uipi_blocked error naming the elevated\nexe/pid/hwnd (blocked_by_uipi:true on the action), under dry_run too -\nthe mode is never silently switched and success is never pretended. A\nSendInput short-send against an elevated foreground is likewise flagged\nblocked_by_uipi:true. list_windows reports elevated per window.\n\nNO-STEAL INPUT GATE (default). target={hwnd?,pid?,exe?,appId?,\ntitleContains?,className?} (or a selector string) locks ONE window for the\nwhole call: acting verbs go UIA-pattern first, then PostMessage/SendMessage\nto that hwnd - no SendInput, no SetCursorPos, no SetForegroundWindow, no\nactivation, foreground or alt-tabbed. The lock is resolved once and\nrevalidated before EVERY action (IsWindow, pid, image name, class); an\nambiguous or vanished target is typed (ambiguous_target / target_gone) and\nNEVER falls back to the foreground window. Without a target every acting verb is refused before anything is sent: target_required for\nkeys; a pointer act (move, click x/y, drag, scroll x/y) returns no_cursor_policy, because the pointer is never moved. Posted message coordinates are signed\n16-bit: anything outside -32768..32767 is refused with bad_coordinates\nbefore a message is posted (never silently truncated). Exact and instant: click is one\nbutton-down + button-up at the point (hover:true is the only way to ask for a\nWM_MOUSEMOVE), drag is down/move/up at exact points, scroll is WM_MOUSEWHEEL\nat the point, type is UIA ValuePattern.SetValue when an element resolves to\nan editable control; plain type/key/hotkey post WM_CHAR/WM_KEYDOWN/WM_SYSKEYDOWN to the locked target (delivery:\"auto\"|\"posted\", verify:true by default) and return target_required without one; delivery:\"sendinput\" is refused.\nUnder target, x/y are CLIENT-area physical pixels (GetClientRect space);\nwithout a target they are virtual-desktop screen pixels. focus_window is refused with no_foreground_policy (focusing IS taking the foreground). Results\ncarry foregroundUnchanged/cursorUnchanged, plus target_locked/target_pid/\ntarget_exe when a lock served the call. target and the legacy background\nselector are alternative locks; target wins when both are given.\nTop-level ok is true only when EVERY action succeeded, and failed counts the\nactions that did not. The burst is continue-always, so isError is true only\nwhen NO action succeeded; a wait_for timeout is never an error.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"actions": {"type": "array", "minItems": 1, "maxItems": 256, "items": {"oneOf": [{"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "move"}, "x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "dx": {"type": "integer"}, "dy": {"type": "integer"}, "relative": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["type"], "anyOf": [{"required": ["x", "y"]}, {"required": ["dx", "dy"]}]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "click"}, "x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "button": {"type": "string"}, "count": {"type": "integer"}, "hover": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "element": {"type": "string"}, "index": {"type": "integer"}, "expect_fp": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "down"}, "button": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "up"}, "button": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "drag"}, "from": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "minItems": 2, "maxItems": 2}, "to": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "minItems": 2, "maxItems": 2}, "button": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type", "from", "to"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "scroll"}, "x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "amount": {"type": "integer"}, "axis": {"type": "string", "enum": ["v", "h"], "default": "v"}, "element": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "type"}, "text": {"type": "string"}, "chunk_chars": {"type": "integer"}, "chunk_ms": {"type": "integer"}, "element": {"type": "string"}, "index": {"type": "integer"}, "expect_fp": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "key"}, "name": {"type": "string"}, "hold_ms": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 60000}, "repeat": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 100}, "gap_ms": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 60000}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "hotkey"}, "keys": {"anyOf": [{"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, {"type": "string"}]}}, "required": ["type", "keys"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "wait"}, "ms": {"type": "integer"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "wait_for"}, "kind": {"type": "string", "enum": ["window_appear", "window_disappear", "pixel", "stable", "element"]}, "selector": {"type": "string"}, "x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "color": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "minItems": 3, "maxItems": 3}, "tolerance": {"type": "integer"}, "region": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "integer"}, "minItems": 4, "maxItems": 4}, "timeout_ms": {"type": "integer"}, "poll_ms": {"type": "integer"}, "window": {"type": "string"}, "element": {"type": "string"}, "state": {"type": "string", "enum": ["appear", "disappear", "enabled", "disabled"], "default": "appear"}}, "required": ["type", "kind"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "focus_window"}, "title": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "hwnd": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "invoke"}, "element": {"type": "string"}, "index": {"type": "integer"}, "expect_fp": {"type": "string"}, "state": {"type": "string", "enum": ["expand", "collapse"]}}, "required": ["type", "element"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "set_value"}, "element": {"type": "string"}, "text": {"type": "string"}, "expect_fp": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type", "element", "text"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "clipboard_set"}, "text": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["type"]}, {"type": "object", "properties": {"type": {"const": "clipboard_get"}}, "required": ["type"]}]}}, "background": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "background_args": {"anyOf": [{"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "focus_guard": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "settle_ms": {"type": "integer", "default": 0}, "dry_run": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "desktop": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string", "enum": ["hidden"]}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "target": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hwnd": {"type": "integer"}, "pid": {"type": "integer"}, "exe": {"type": "string"}, "appId": {"type": "string"}, "titleContains": {"type": "string"}, "className": {"type": "string"}}}, {"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "allow_foreground": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "allow_cursor": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "allow_clipboard": {"type": "boolean", "default": false, "description": "Retained for schema compatibility and buys nothing: it would permit overwriting the owner's global clipboard, and clipboard_set is refused with no_clipboard_policy before OpenClipboard whatever this is set to. Reads (clipboard_get) never need it, and a refused call touches no clipboard."}}, "required": ["actions"]}, "name": "do", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"ok": {"type": "boolean"}, "failed": {"type": "integer"}, "results": {"type": "array"}, "total_ms": {"type": "number"}, "sendinput_calls": {"type": "integer"}, "sendinput_ms": {"type": "number"}, "events": {"type": "integer"}, "focus_before": {"type": "integer"}, "focus_after": {"type": "integer"}, "foregroundUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "cursorUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "target_locked": {"type": "integer"}, "target_pid": {"type": "integer"}, "target_exe": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["results", "total_ms", "sendinput_calls", "sendinput_ms", "events", "focus_before", "focus_after"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Do", "annotations": {"title": "Do", "readOnlyHint": false, "destructiveHint": true, "idempotentHint": false, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_CURSOR: &str = r#"{"description": "Current cursor position + monitor rects as JSON:\n{x, y, screens:[[l,t,r,b],...]}.", "inputSchema": {"properties": {}, "type": "object", "additionalProperties": false}, "name": "cursor", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"x": {"type": "integer"}, "y": {"type": "integer"}, "screens": {"type": "array"}}, "required": ["x", "y", "screens"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Cursor", "annotations": {"title": "Cursor", "readOnlyHint": true, "destructiveHint": false, "idempotentHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
pub const TOOL_ELEMENTS: &str = r#"{"description": "List structured UI elements for a window as JSON, zero-pixel (no screenshot, no focus change, no input).\nTarget by selector (title text or hwnd; the same TargetLock as target:). detail=true keeps the raw win and hwnd fields on each entry; default false returns the compact {ref,role,name,auto_id,rect,offscreen,invokable,path,fp} shape, omitting win (and hwnd on the Win32 fallback).\nEach entry carries a ref token \"<hwnd>.<path>\" (e.g. \"199210.0.3.1\"): a per-enumeration identifier for correlating entries between two listings, not a durable handle and not an identity guarantee - invoke re-enumerates and matches name:|auto_id:|path:, so a ref from an older listing can address a different control if the UI changed in between. Invoke accepts name:, auto_id:, and path: only; there is no ref-based invoke selector.\nReturns JSON {backend,truncated,rect_space,elements,uia_available,\nuia_error,fallback,empty[,empty_reason],depth_capped,depth_limit}, the same top-level object the screenshot elements block carries (per-entry shapes differ as above).\nEach entry carries fp, a stable identity fingerprint (FNV-1a over\nrole/name/auto_id/invokable, 16 hex chars); the compact default shape\nis {ref,role,name,auto_id,rect,offscreen,invokable,path,fp}. offscreen:true\nmarks a control whose rect has no area (a zero or negative width/height): the\nrect is kept for shape stability but is not geometry to aim at, and click\nrefuses it with offscreen_element. invoke accepts\nan optional expect_fp alongside any name:/auto_id:/path: selector: when the\nre-walked entry's fp differs, the action refuses with ok:false, resolution\nstale and a stale_ref error advising a fresh elements snapshot, instead of\nacting on whatever now sits at that selector. max_depth (1..32, default 8)\nbounds the UIA walk depth (controls deeper than the cut-off set depth_capped);\noffset (default 0) skips that many leading controls for paging. When the\n200-entry cap is hit and more controls remain, next_offset carries the offset\nof the next page, else null. With detail:true, UIA-backend entries also carry\ntext (TextPattern document text, capped at 4000 chars) plus text_truncated;\nentries without readable text omit both keys. Text never participates in fp.\n\ntarget={hwnd?,pid?,exe?,appId?,titleContains?,className?} (or a selector\nstring) locks ONE top-level window for the call (wins over title/hwnd) and\nis revalidated; an ambiguous/vanished target is typed (ambiguous_target /\ntarget_gone) and never falls back to the foreground window. The walk is\nread-only: no capture, no input, no focus change, no pointer move.\nforegroundUnchanged/cursorUnchanged report the measured before/after\ninvariant.", "inputSchema": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"title": {"anyOf": [{"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "hwnd": {"anyOf": [{"type": "integer"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}, "detail": {"type": "boolean", "default": false}, "max_depth": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 32, "default": 8}, "offset": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 0, "default": 0}, "target": {"anyOf": [{"type": "object", "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hwnd": {"type": "integer"}, "pid": {"type": "integer"}, "exe": {"type": "string"}, "appId": {"type": "string"}, "titleContains": {"type": "string"}, "className": {"type": "string"}}}, {"type": "string"}, {"type": "null"}], "default": null}}, "anyOf": [{"required": ["title"]}, {"required": ["hwnd"]}, {"required": ["target"]}]}, "name": "elements", "outputSchema": {"type": "object", "properties": {"backend": {"type": "string"}, "truncated": {"type": "boolean"}, "rect_space": {"type": "string"}, "elements": {"type": "array"}, "uia_available": {"type": "boolean"}, "uia_error": {}, "fallback": {}, "empty": {"type": "boolean"}, "empty_reason": {"type": "string"}, "depth_capped": {"type": "boolean"}, "depth_limit": {"type": "integer"}, "foregroundUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}, "cursorUnchanged": {"type": "boolean"}}, "required": ["backend", "truncated", "rect_space", "elements", "uia_available", "empty", "depth_capped", "depth_limit"], "additionalProperties": true}, "title": "Elements", "annotations": {"title": "Elements", "readOnlyHint": true, "destructiveHint": false, "idempotentHint": true, "openWorldHint": false}}"#;
